  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Cocosamide B and DMS-273 through a series of target interactions. Cocosamide B is implicated in targeting Tankyrase-2 and HepG2, both of which are targets of a compound with the structure (3R)-5,8,9-trimethoxy-2,2-dimethyl-3,4-dihydropyrano[2,3-b]quinolin-3-ol. This compound, in turn, has a target of DMS-273. Similarly, Cocosamide B is also shown to target Hepatocyte, which is a target of another compound, 3-(1H-Benzimidazol-2-Yl)-7-(Diethylamino)Chromen-2-One, which also targets DMS-273. These findings collectively indicate that Cocosamide B may interact with various molecular targets that ultimately lead to a relationship with DMS-273. The evidence is consistent across different pathways, suggesting a possible mechanism involving the inhibition of specific enzymes or proteins that are involved in cellular processes affecting DMS-273. However, the exact nature of the interaction and its relevance to DMS-273 remains to be fully elucidated."
